# Web UI taps (kingfisher cockpit)

Live sensor DOM updates can block `click` on iPad/WebKit. **Do not use bare `click` listeners** for interactive controls.

Use `KFTap` from `internal/web/static/tap.js` (loaded before `app.js` / `howgozit.js`):

| Control | API |
|---------|-----|
| Buttons, nav, list rows | `KFTap.bindPress(root, selector, handler)` |
| Live-updating list rows | add `{ stableKey: 'device', slop: 12 }` (matches `data-device` via `dataset.device`) |
| One-off buttons | `KFTap.bindTap(el, handler)` |
| Dialog / form field focus | `KFTap.bindFieldFocus(container, fieldSelector, inputSelector)` — focus on `pointerdown`; use `KFTap.focusFormControl(el)` for programmatic focus |
| Dialog Cancel/Close | `KFTap.wireDialogCloses()` at init |
| Checkboxes in `label.cfgCheckbox` | `KFTap.wireCheckboxLabels()` at init |
| Dialog Save (async) | `type="button"` + `KFTap.bindPress(form, '[data-…-save]', …)` — not native `type="submit"` |

**Dialogs:** define `<dialog>` in `index.html` as a direct `<body>` child (same as Settings/More), not inside `#main` / `#howgozitMount`.

**CSS:** `touch-action: manipulation` and `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` on tappable controls.

**While a dialog is open:** `app.js` skips live overview re-renders (`modalOpen()`); do not add per-frame DOM rewrites that overlap open dialogs.
